{"reviewer_participant_id":"actor:dependence-free-batch-f2-reviewer-fable-30","reviews":[{"case_id":"case:b24355b160cf4665b929","verdict":"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope","bounded_statement":null,"root_cause":null,"issue_class":null,"evidence_atoms":[{"description":"The data description names vessel_id as the independent-unit column and states that each vessel appears five times as repeated weekly measures, so any valid ration-level inference must rest on 12 vessel-level values.","observed_value":"12 independent vessels, 5 repeated rows each","source_spans":[{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":5,"end_line":6,"quoted_text":"One row is: one weekly headspace gas sample taken from one digester vessel in one run week\nIndependent unit column: vessel_id"}]},{"description":"The workflow collapses each vessel's weekly series to a single vessel-level mean before any statistical test, producing exactly one value per independent unit.","observed_value":"one mean per vessel_id","source_spans":[{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":48,"end_line":51,"quoted_text":"    return [\n        (vessel, blend_of[vessel], len(values), float(np.mean(values)))\n        for vessel, values in weekly.items()\n    ]"}]},{"description":"The Mann-Whitney U test is applied to the lists 'test' and 'reference', which are built from the vessel-level means (one entry per vessel), not from the 60 raw rows.","observed_value":"test inputs: 6 enriched vessel means vs 6 standard vessel means","source_spans":[{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":135,"end_line":142,"quoted_text":"    vessels = average_within_vessel(records)\n    reference = [mean for _, blend, _, mean in vessels if blend == REFERENCE_BLEND]\n    test = [mean for _, blend, _, mean in vessels if blend == TEST_BLEND]\n    if not reference or not test:\n        raise ValueError(\"both feed blends must be present in the table\")\n    outcome = stats.mannwhitneyu(\n        test, reference, alternative=\"two-sided\", method=\"exact\"\n    )"}]},{"description":"The report's selected result states the test was computed from one averaged value per vessel with n = 6 per blend, and the reported U = 35 and p = 0.0043 are exactly reproducible from the 12 vessel means: the sole cross-group inversion is D11 (61.22) above D02 (60.96), giving U = 35 and exact two-sided p = 4/924 = 0.0043.","observed_value":"U = 35, exact two-sided p = 4/924 ≈ 0.0043, n = 6 vessels per group","source_spans":[{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":35,"end_line":37,"quoted_text":"- exact two-sided Mann-Whitney U = 35, p = 0.0043\n\n[selected-result] Enriched-feed digesters held a higher headspace methane fraction than standard-feed digesters: median vessel mean 62.22 % versus 59.58 % (+2.64 percentage points), exact two-sided Mann-Whitney U = 35, p = 0.0043, computed from one averaged value per vessel for 6 enriched and 6 standard vessels."},{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":11,"end_line":11,"quoted_text":"Each vessel's weekly series was therefore averaged into a single vessel-level methane fraction, and the blend contrast was tested on those 12 independent vessel values with an exact two-sided Mann-Whitney U test (6 standard vessels versus 6 enriched vessels, no ties among the vessel means)."}]}],"counterevidence_atoms":[{"description":"The precondition for the issue is present: the stored table holds 60 vessel-week rows (5 repeated rows per authorized independent unit), and the workflow reads all 60 rows verbatim, so per-row entry into the test was possible. However, these repeated rows only reach the aggregation step, not the test itself.","observed_value":"60 rows read; 12 values tested","source_spans":[{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":18,"end_line":18,"quoted_text":"The file has 60 data rows: 12 vessels multiplied by 5 weekly samples. Any statement made at the ration level rests on 12 values, one per vessel, rather than on the 60 stored rows."},{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":7,"end_line":7,"quoted_text":"The stored table holds 60 vessel-week rows for 12 vessels, 5 weekly samples per vessel."}]}],"falsification_attempt":"I tried to show the issue was present by testing whether the reported statistics could only arise from per-row entry of the 60 vessel-week rows. I recomputed all 12 vessel means by hand from data/input.csv (e.g., D01 = 293.4/5 = 58.68; D12 = 317.6/5 = 63.52) and they match the report's table exactly. I then recomputed the exact Mann-Whitney on those 12 means: the only enriched-vs-standard pair where the standard vessel wins is D11 (61.22) over D02 (60.96), so U = 6*6 - 1 = 35, and the exact two-sided p is 4/924 ≈ 0.004329, which rounds to the reported 0.0043. A row-level test on 30-vs-30 rows would have reported n = 30 per group and a far smaller p with complete or near-complete separation; the report instead states n = 6 vessels per blend and even notes the ~0.002 minimum attainable p for a 6-vs-6 exact rank test, which is only true at the vessel level. The falsification attempt failed: every reported number is consistent with, and reproducible from, one value per independent unit.","cross_case_evidence_used":false,"unresolved_material_questions":[],"self_reported_confidence":"high"}]}